## Integration Tests with Docker

A local PostgreSQL database can be started with:

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

Once the database is healthy, run the full test suite (including integration
tests) with:

```bash
uv run inv test
```

Integration tests that require the database use the `db_connection` fixture
from `tests/conftest.py`. They are automatically skipped when the database is
not reachable, so the unit-test suite can always run without Docker.

### Loading CSV Data

Place CSV files in `tests/data/`. Each file must be named after the target
table (e.g. `records.csv` populates the `records` table). The database
container loads these files automatically on first start via
`docker/postgres/init/02_load_csv.sh`.

To reload data after modifying the CSVs:

```bash
docker compose down -v   # removes the named volume
docker compose up -d     # recreates and reloads
```
